Provides:
 ${vinyld:ABI},
 ${vinyld:VRT},
 ${vinyld:COHORT},
Suggests: vinyl-cache-dev
Description: state of the art, high-performance web accelerator
 Vinyl Cache is a state of the art web accelerator written with performance
 and flexibility in mind. It stores web pages in memory so web servers do not
 have to create the same page over and over again.
 .
 This package contains the vinyld daemon, the command line utilities, the
 shared library, the VMODs distributed with Vinyl Cache, and the systemd
 service integration.
 .
 The package also provides three virtual packages that identify the exact VMOD
 binary interface of this build: vinyld-vrt, carrying the public VRT ABI
 version, vinyld-abi-<hash>, carrying the exact strict VMOD ABI, and
 vinyld-cohort-<cohort-id>, carrying the identity of the coordinated package
 cohort this runtime was built and tested as part of. A VMOD that declares
 "$ABI strict" depends on all three, so an incompatible Vinyl Cache upgrade is
 unresolvable rather than silently loadable.
 .
 The cohort provide exists because the ABI provide cannot police provenance.
 vinyld-abi-<hash> is derived from the upstream source revision, so two
 packages built from the same revision with different downstream patches, a
 different build profile or a vendor respin advertise the identical token and
 are interchangeable as far as apt is concerned. The cohort id is a digest of
 the pinned source archive, the ordered patch series and the production build
 profile, so a package from a different cohort no longer satisfies an installed
 VMOD's dependency even when it claims the same ABI.
 .
 EXPERIMENTAL: this is a pre-9.0.0 snapshot package built from an unreleased
 development revision. It carries no security-update commitment.

Package: vinyl-cache-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 vinyl-cache (= ${binary:Version}),
 pkgconf,
 python3,
Description: development files for Vinyl Cache
 Vinyl Cache is a state of the art web accelerator written with performance
 and flexibility in mind.
 .
 This package contains the headers, the vinylapi.pc pkg-config file, the
 vinyl.m4 autoconf macros and the vmodtool.py and vsctool.py generators
 needed to build a Vinyl Cache VMOD or an application against libvinylapi.
 .
 Because a strict-ABI VMOD is bound to one exact Vinyl Cache build, this
 package depends on the exact matching vinyl-cache binary version rather than
 on a version range.
 .
 EXPERIMENTAL: this is a pre-9.0.0 snapshot package built from an unreleased
 development revision. It carries no security-update commitment.
